## runner start
OVERVIEW: Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android) and keep it alive
for interactive use.

## runner
OVERVIEW: Manage the embedded UI automation runner.

USAGE: grantiva runner <subcommand>
--
  start                   Start the runner with WDA (UIAutomator2 on Android)
                          and keep it alive for interactive use.
  stop                    Stop the running runner session.
## runner dump-hierarchy
OVERVIEW: Dump the view hierarchy from a running app for agent inspection.

USAGE: grantiva runner dump-hierarchy [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--port <port>] [--format <format>] [--udid <udid>]

OPTIONS:
--
  -p, --port <port>       Driver port: WDA on iOS, the forwarded UIAutomator2
                          port on Android (auto-detected from the active
                          session if omitted)
## hierarchy
OVERVIEW: Dump the UI hierarchy of a booted simulator or emulator without
relaunching the app.

--
USAGE: grantiva hierarchy [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] [--udid <udid>] [--timeout <timeout>] [--format <format>]

OPTIONS:
--
  --timeout <timeout>     Seconds to wait for GrantivaAgent's (iOS) or
                          UIAutomator2's (Android) page-source response.
                          Default: 60. (default: 60.0)
## run
OVERVIEW: Run Maestro flows against a simulator or emulator. No visual
regression — reports step pass/fail and captures a screenshot on failure.

--
  --app-file <app-file>   Path to a pre-built app: .app bundle or .ipa archive
                          (iOS), .apk (Android). Skips the build step.
  --no-build              Skip building and installing — assume the app is
                          already on the device. With --app-file, that file is
                          installed (only the build is skipped).
  --derived-data-path <derived-data-path>
--
  --timeout <timeout>     Max seconds to wait for the runner subprocess before
                          killing it with SIGTERM. Default: 600 (10 min).
                          Minimum 30. Ignored under --keep-alive. Bump this for
## build install
OVERVIEW: Build and install the app on a simulator or emulator, then optionally
launch it.

--
  --app-file <app-file>   Path to a pre-built app: .app bundle or .ipa archive
                          (iOS), .apk (Android). Skips the build step.
  --no-build              Skip building and installing — assume the app is
                          already on the device. With --app-file, that file is
                          installed (only the build is skipped).
  --derived-data-path <derived-data-path>
## diff capture
OVERVIEW: Navigate to configured screens and capture screenshots.

USAGE: grantiva diff capture <options>
--
  --app-file <app-file>   Path to a pre-built app: .app bundle or .ipa archive
                          (iOS), .apk (Android). Skips the build step.
  --no-build              Skip building and installing — assume the app is
                          already on the device. With --app-file, that file is
                          installed (only the build is skipped).
  --derived-data-path <derived-data-path>
## ci run
OVERVIEW: Run full CI pipeline: capture screenshots, compare against baselines,
upload results.

--
  --app-file <app-file>   Path to a pre-built app: .app bundle or .ipa archive
                          (iOS), .apk (Android). Skips the build step.
  --no-build              Skip building and installing — assume the app is
                          already on the device. With --app-file, that file is
                          installed (only the build is skipped).
  --derived-data-path <derived-data-path>
